    <!--
      The isolate characters around the signed offsets are deliberate: a leading "+" or "-" is
      bidirectionally neutral, so in a Hebrew layout it migrates to the far side and "-1d" is
      drawn as "1d-". U+2066/U+2069 keep each one whole (NFR-UX-08).
